  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "Aufer a nobis is said quietly as the priest ascends to the altar. Orámus te follows at the altar, with a kiss of the altar during the prayer. The first petition uses the plural nobis and nostras. The second ends by asking forgiveness for ómnia peccáta mea, all my sins. The introductory Orémus is said aloud. Its punctuation differs between the witnesses, as recorded in the apparatus. Sancta sanctórum names the Holy of Holies. Both words are substantivized neuter adjectives, with the second in the genitive plural. Quǽsumus is a defective verb used here as a parenthetical request, entered under quæso.",
    "source": {
      "method": "Read word by word from the page image of the Benziger Brothers 1962 Editio iuxta typicam, which the Missal witness below transcribes, and collated against the other witnesses: zero substantive divergence. All accidental variants are declared in the apparatus.",
